{"title":"Career Roadmap · Special Education Support","role":"Special Education Support","summary":"Special Education Support is an interdisciplinary career focused on helping children and adolescents with developmental, learning, sensory, motor, communication, behavioral, or functional difficulties participate more effectively in education and daily life.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Occupational Therapy (BOT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Special Education Support is an interdisciplinary career focused on helping children and adolescents with developmental, learning, sensory, motor, communication, behavioral, or functional difficulties participate more effectively in education and daily life."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BOT graduate, the strongest positioning is at the intersection of occupational therapy + educational participation + developmental rehabilitation."},{"type":"p","text":"A BOT professional may support students with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Autism spectrum conditions"},{"text":"ADHD"},{"text":"Developmental delays"},{"text":"Intellectual disabilities"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Learning difficulties"},{"text":"Sensory processing challenges"},{"text":"Fine- and gross-motor difficulties"},{"text":"Handwriting difficulties"},{"text":"Self-care limitations"},{"text":"Classroom participation challenges"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The professional role should remain within the scope of occupational therapy and applicable professional/education regulations. Where a position specifically requires a recognized special educator qualification, BOT alone should not be treated as automatically equivalent to that qualification."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BOT","Clinical Internship","Pediatric / Developmental OT Exposure","Occupational Therapist","Special Education / School-Based Rehabilitation Experience","Advanced Training in Pediatric & Developmental OT","School-Based / Special Education Support Professional","Senior Pediatric OT / Inclusion Consultant"]},{"type":"p","text":"A complementary special-education qualification can be valuable when the target role requires formal special-educator credentials."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"BOT Years 1–2"},{"text":"Human development, anatomy, psychology and OT foundations"}],[{"text":"BOT Years 3–4"},{"text":"Pediatric OT, developmental conditions and clinical assessment"}],[{"text":"Clinical Internship"},{"text":"Supervised pediatric and rehabilitation practice"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Pediatric occupational therapy and school-based intervention"}],[{"text":"Advanced Career"},{"text":"Individualized education support and multidisciplinary coordination"}],[{"text":"Senior Career"},{"text":"Inclusion consulting, program development and clinical leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic Focus"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Introduction to occupational therapy"},{"text":"Basic health sciences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Develop"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation skills"},{"text":"Child-friendly communication"},{"text":"Basic documentation"},{"text":"Professional ethics"},{"text":"Understanding of developmental milestones"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand typical development in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motor skills"},{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Social interaction"},{"text":"Emotional development"},{"text":"Self-care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Occupational Therapy Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Occupational therapy assessment"},{"text":"Activity analysis"},{"text":"Therapeutic activities"},{"text":"Functional training"},{"text":"Mental health fundamentals"},{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Pediatric rehabilitation fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core OT Concept"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should learn to analyze:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Child","Abilities & Challenges","Occupational Demands","Environmental Barriers","Participation Problem","OT Intervention","Functional Outcome"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Pediatric & Developmental OT"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important stage for this career."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pediatric occupational therapy"},{"text":"Developmental disabilities"},{"text":"Autism"},{"text":"ADHD"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Intellectual disability"},{"text":"Developmental coordination difficulties"},{"text":"Sensory-motor development"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Family-centered practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to assess:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fine motor skills"},{"text":"Gross motor abilities"},{"text":"Visual-motor integration"},{"text":"Hand-eye coordination"},{"text":"Bilateral coordination"},{"text":"Postural control"},{"text":"Sensory responses"},{"text":"Self-care skills"},{"text":"Play skills"},{"text":"School participation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — School-Based Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from clinical treatment toward participation and educational support."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classroom participation"},{"text":"Handwriting support"},{"text":"Fine-motor intervention"},{"text":"Seating and positioning"},{"text":"Assistive devices"},{"text":"Sensory/environmental adaptations"},{"text":"Activities of daily living"},{"text":"Social participation"},{"text":"Functional communication support"},{"text":"Parent education"},{"text":"Teacher collaboration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example Case Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Referral","Child & Family Interview","Developmental / Functional Assessment","Occupational Profile","School Participation Analysis","Identify Barriers","Set Functional Goals","Intervention Plan","Teacher + Parent Collaboration","Progress Measurement"]}]},{"heading":"Clinical Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize rotations/exposure in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pediatric Hospitals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Developmental pediatrics"},{"text":"Neurology"},{"text":"Orthopaedics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Child Development Centers"},{"type":"p","text":"Exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Autism"},{"text":"ADHD"},{"text":"Developmental delays"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Intellectual disability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Schools"},{"type":"p","text":"Seek school-based experience involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Special education"},{"text":"Classroom accommodations"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Student participation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation Centers"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multidisciplinary rehabilitation"},{"text":"Speech therapy"},{"text":"Physiotherapy"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Special education"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Competency Framework","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A. Child Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop competency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental screening"},{"text":"Occupational profile"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Fine-motor assessment"},{"text":"Gross-motor observation"},{"text":"Sensory processing assessment"},{"text":"Visual-perceptual assessment"},{"text":"ADL assessment"},{"text":"School participation assessment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"B. Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to design interventions around:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fine-motor development"},{"text":"Handwriting"},{"text":"Dressing"},{"text":"Feeding"},{"text":"Grooming"},{"text":"Play"},{"text":"Classroom participation"},{"text":"Motor planning"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Sensory regulation"},{"text":"Functional independence"}]}]},{"heading":"Special Education Support Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A BOT graduate targeting this field should understand the principles of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Individualized Support"},{"type":"flow","items":["Student Needs","Functional Assessment","Priority Areas","Individual Goals","Classroom Strategies","Home Strategies","Progress Review"]},{"type":"h","text":"Classroom Support"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Seating"},{"text":"Desk positioning"},{"text":"Writing tools"},{"text":"Classroom organization"},{"text":"Movement breaks"},{"text":"Visual schedules"},{"text":"Task simplification"},{"text":"Environmental modifications"},{"text":"Assistive technology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These strategies should be individualized rather than applying the same intervention to every child with a particular diagnosis."}]},{"heading":"Sensory & Functional Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Arousal/regulation"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Motor planning"},{"text":"Classroom participation"},{"text":"Self-care"},{"text":"Play"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal should be functional participation, not simply reducing a behavior without understanding its context."}]},{"heading":"Communication & Collaboration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Special education support is highly multidisciplinary."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parents"},{"text":"Special educators"},{"text":"General classroom teachers"},{"text":"Speech-language professionals"},{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Psychologists"},{"text":"Pediatricians"},{"text":"Developmental specialists"},{"text":"School administrators"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to convert clinical observations into practical educational recommendations."},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Poor fine-motor coordination.\""},{"type":"p","text":"A stronger professional communication style is:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"The student has difficulty maintaining a functional pencil grasp and manipulating small classroom materials, which affects writing and task completion.\""}]},{"heading":"Technology & Assistive Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Important technology areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AAC systems"},{"text":"Adaptive keyboards"},{"text":"Alternative mice"},{"text":"Pencil grips"},{"text":"Writing aids"},{"text":"Seating systems"},{"text":"Mobility aids"},{"text":"Visual scheduling applications"},{"text":"Educational accessibility tools"},{"text":"Speech-to-text"},{"text":"Text-to-speech"},{"text":"Digital learning tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted educational personalization"},{"text":"Computer vision for movement analysis"},{"text":"Digital developmental assessments"},{"text":"Wearable monitoring"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Adaptive learning platforms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Technology should complement individualized professional assessment."}]},{"heading":"Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Occupational therapy assessment"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Pediatric OT"},{